  data:  # f2fe
    kind: invariant  # f2fe
    title: "Go field-chain and chained-return-type receiver arms bind the first global candidate for a bare Type.Method key, whatever its package"  # f2fe
    status: violated  # f2fe
    priority: 3  # f2fe
    parent:  # f2fe
    tags:  # f2fe
    - analysis_quality  # f2fe
    - call_resolution  # f2fe
    - go  # f2fe
    isbefore: []  # f2fe
    duplicate_of: []  # f2fe
    not_duplicate_of: []  # f2fe
    pr_ref:  # f2fe
    description: "Found by the 2026-10-05 docstring staleness audit (code read, not yet reproduced on a corpus). The SDConfig.UnmarshalYAML case that motivated _go_method_of_type (every package's SDConfig shared one key) applies equally when the receiver is reached through a struct field or a call's declared return type. Repro to write: two packages each defining Config.Load, a struct field typed with the second package's Config, a call through the field. go.py's module docstring now states the gap."  # f2fe
    fields:  # f2fe
      statement: "A typed receiver's method binds to the method of the receiver's own type in that type's package (the _go_method_of_type rule)."  # f2fe
      root_cause: "Symbols are keyed by unqualified Type.Method. The typed-local and method-value arms use _go_method_of_type, but the field-chain arm (go.py ~L4417-4420) and the chained-return-type arm (~L4556-4559) do 'target = candidates[0]' from global_symbols."  # f2fe
- op: discuss  # c4a8
  at: '2026-10-16T08:01:04Z'  # c4a8
  by: agent  # c4a8
  actor: jgstern_agent  # c4a8
  clock: 2  # c4a8
  nonce: c4a8  # c4a8
  message: "Reproduced a sibling case 2026-10-16 (docstring audit): the field-chain arm also binds an in-repo method when the field's type is KNOWN EXTERNAL. Temp module: mylog/logger.go declares (*Logger).Info; app/engine.go has type Engine struct{ logger *slog.Logger } and calls e.logger.Info(\"hi\"). analyze_go emits Engine.Run -> go:mylog/logger.go:5-5:Logger.Info:method, meta receiver=typed_field, confidence 0.85. Cause: go.py ~4451-4461 does the bare local/global lookup before the _external_package_for_type check in the elif (~4478-4492). go.py's docstring L64-67 states the intended rule (never looked up in-repo); fix order: external check first, then the package-scoped lookup this item already asks for."  # c4a8
